# Wave W17-AB (Foamline Path): foam rock — shallows footing rock: a pale sun-bleached boulder standing in bright shallows, foam collar thick at its base where the walkway’s feet meet the sea (design: the plank road runs over bright water; its footings stand in the foam the path is named for). Foamline’s own rock — split from Route 218’s footing rock by depth entire (bright shallows vs harbour water) and from Route 223’s cliff rock by face: sun-bleached pale here, basalt-dark there.
